    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Weapon (Greatsword, Longsword, Rapier, Scimitar, or Shortsword), Rarity Varies (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>This weapon is covered in oceanic motifs, from wavelike etchings on its blade to stylized sea monsters embroidered onto its leather hilt.</p><p><strong>Barnacled (Uncommon).</strong> Barnacles dot this blade’s guard and the flat sides of its etched blade.</p><p>You have a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. While holding this weapon, you can take a Magic action to touch up to a gallon of liquid and infuse it with brine, turning fresh water into saltwater, for instance.</p><p><strong>Aquatic (Rare).</strong> The wavelike etchings on this weapon’s blade glow with light, shedding Bright Light in a 5-foot radius and Dim Light for an additional 5 feet.</p><p>Your bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon increases to +2. While you hold the weapon, you can breathe underwater, and you have a Swim Speed of 30 feet.</p><p><strong>Ascendant (Very Rare).</strong> The sea monsters embroidered on this weapon’s hilt are studded with chips of colorful gemstones.</p><p>Your bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon increases to +3. While you hold this weapon, you have a Fly Speed of 30 feet; when you use this Fly Speed, a salty sea breeze carries you through the air.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-gYN5xhL6EngFd0YJ\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Glissez l’enchantement de l’état de l’arme (Barnacled, Aquatic ou Ascendant) sur l’arme voulue : elle garde son nom, sa rareté et son prix. Chaque état garde les propriétés des précédents. Quand l’arme évolue, retirez l’enchantement dans son onglet <em>Effects</em> et appliquez le suivant.</p></section><p>@Embed[Compendium.dnd5e.content24.JournalEntry.dmgFoundryRefere.JournalEntryPage.Ok4iCgD25ENgoRxE cite=false caption=false classes=\"hide-in-embed\"]</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
